kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "app-tui"
purpose: "TBD - created by archiving change c325-add-app-tui-spec. Update purpose after archive."
valid_scope[2]: src/,tests/
requirements[17]{req_id,title,statement}:
  tui1,"inline-render","The TUI MUST render inline using ratatui Viewport::Inline with Terminal::insert_before to commit finalized lines to the terminal scrollback; the TUI MUST NOT enter the alternate screen (no ?1049h). Evidence: ratatui 0.30.2 insert_before is a stable public API (ratatui-core-0.1.2/src/terminal/inline.rs:109); pi renders inline with no alt-screen (grep of packages/tui/src finds ?1049h only in external-editor cleanup); codex is inline too."
  tui2,"in-process-driver","The TUI MUST drive the agent via app::core::driver::InProcessDriver (the same Driver path as print mode); the TUI MUST NOT default to a RemoteDriver or an auto-spawned daemon. Evidence: codex AppServerTarget::Embedded is the TUI default (codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs:814-830); pi InteractiveMode holds AgentSessionRuntime directly (coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts:265,391)."
  tui3,"three-surfaces-coexist","The rpc (stdio JSONL), server (REST+WS), and tui (inline) application surfaces MUST coexist; none MAY be removed in the name of unification. Evidence: codex keeps in-process TUI + app-server stdio (powers VSCode ext) + app-server-daemon (unix socket); pi keeps in-process TUI + --mode rpc + orchestrator serve; neither project dropped any transport."
  tui4,"reuse-contract","The TUI MUST import only crate::agent (mod-level), crate::app::core (Driver/composition), crate::protocol, and crate::domain; it MUST NOT import crate::agent::session, crate::agent::runtime, or crate::infra. Slash command semantics MUST reuse protocol::Command variants rather than inventing a parallel command vocabulary."
  tui5,"no-skeleton-spray","Every file created under src/app/tui/ MUST be driven by a real entry point (tui::run) within its own change; the TUI MUST NOT use #[allow(dead_code)] to land undriven skeleton code. Undriven skeleton is the documented root cause of the prior two failed TUI attempts."
  tui10,"repl-entry","The CLI MUST dispatch to app::tui::run when no prompt is provided and stdin is a TTY (mirroring pi resolveAppMode), entering an inline REPL driven by InProcessDriver; a --tui flag MAY force the TUI even with a prompt."
  tui11,"event-loop","The TUI MUST run a tokio::select! event loop multiplexing three sources: the XyEvent stream from Driver::run, crossterm keyboard input via EventStream (requires crossterm event-stream feature), and a cancellation signal that calls Driver::abort."
  tui12,"inline-render-pipeline","The TUI MUST render finalized content to the scrollback via Terminal::insert_before and redraw only the mutable tail (current streaming line, spinner, tool status) via Terminal::draw over a Viewport::Inline region; the tail MUST be freely redrawable each frame without disturbing committed scrollback."
  tui13,"xyevent-coverage","The TUI render MUST handle at minimum these XyEvent variants: TextDelta (stream to tail then commit on boundary), ThinkingDelta, ToolExecutionStart/Update/End, ModelSelect, Error, TurnStart/TurnEnd; unhandled variants MUST degrade gracefully (e.g. log) not panic."
  tui14,"slash-commands","The TUI MUST parse slash commands /exit (maps to Quit) and /model (maps to SetModel or CycleModel) reusing protocol::Command semantics; unknown slash input MUST show an inline error not crash."
  tui15,"terminal-lifecycle","The TUI MUST enable raw mode and Viewport::Inline on entry and MUST restore the terminal on exit via Drop or explicit teardown even on panic or error, so the user's terminal is never left in a broken raw-mode state."
  tui20,"core-backend-direct","The TUI MUST depend on ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm directly (NOT the umbrella ratatui crate); the umbrella ratatui dependency MUST be removed from Cargo.toml. Evidence: ratatui-core v0.1.2 contains all types used (Terminal/Frame/Viewport::Inline/insert_before/set_cursor_position/Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Line/Span/Widget trait) at ratatui/ratatui-core/src/; umbrella init.rs convenience (try_init_with_options/restore/DefaultTerminal) is ~15 lines replicated locally. ratatui-crossterm provides CrosstermBackend (ratatui/ratatui-crossterm/src/lib.rs:160)."
  tui21,"no-builtin-widgets","The TUI MUST NOT use any ratatui built-in widget (Paragraph/Block/List/Table/etc.); components MUST be hand-rolled using Line::render (Line implements Widget at ratatui-core/src/text/line.rs:699) or direct Buffer manipulation. Evidence: codex hand-rolls via its own Renderable trait + direct buf.set_string (codex-rs/tui/src/render/renderable.rs:22, bottom_pane/textarea.rs:1928); pi/kimi-code hand-roll all components with no widget toolkit. Built-in widgets target alt-screen full repaint, not inline mutable-tail+scrollback."
  tui22,"scrolling-regions","The TUI MUST enable the ratatui-core scrolling-regions feature (forwarded via ratatui-crossterm) to reduce insert_before flicker; this addresses the c340 §7 known-leftover insert_before jelly effect."
  tui30,"user-message-echo","The TUI MUST commit the user's submitted prompt text to the scrollback immediately on Enter (before or during driver.run), styled distinctly (e.g. ❯ prefix) so the user sees their own message in the conversation history. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #3 noted user input never reached scrollback; pi/kimi-code user-message components (kimi-code/apps/kimi-code/src/tui/components/messages/user-message.ts) echo user input on submit."
  tui31,"turn-end-flush-consistent","The TUI MUST flush the final streaming line to scrollback and clear the tail in the same frame on TurnEnd, so no reply text lingers in the mutable tail after a turn completes. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #4 noted the last reply line stayed in the tail until the next submit."
  tui32,"input-anchored-visual","The TUI input region MUST appear visually anchored to the bottom (no floating/gap错觉); unused tail rows MUST be filled (background block or divider) so the input area reads as a continuous bottom-anchored region. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #1 noted Viewport::Inline(3) left a perceived gap; kimi-code footer uses background fill."
scenarios[22]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui1,"inline-viewport",the TUI source is inspected,"Viewport::Inline is used and insert_before commits finalized lines",no EnterAlternateScreen/?1049h is emitted and history remains in the terminal scrollback
  tui1,"scrollback-copy",a conversation turn finishes in the TUI,the user scrolls up in the terminal,prior turns are visible in the native scrollback and selectable with the terminal native selection
  tui2,"inprocess-default",xylitol is launched with no prompt and stdin is a TTY,the TUI starts,the agent is driven via InProcessDriver not RemoteDriver
  tui3,"rpc-retained",the rpc surface is inspected after the TUI lands,"--rpc dispatch and src/app/rpc.rs are checked",rpc mode is still present and functional
  tui3,"server-retained",the server surface is inspected after the TUI lands,xylitol server run and src/app/server are checked,the server is still present and functional
  tui4,"no-infra-import",the TUI source is inspected,imports under src/app/tui are checked,"none import crate::agent::session crate::agent::runtime or crate::infra and slash commands map to protocol::Command"
  tui5,"driven-on-land",a file is added under src/app/tui,it is checked at change completion,"it is reachable from tui::run and has no #[allow(dead_code)]"
  tui10,"tty-default",xylitol is run with no arguments and stdin is a TTY,the process starts,"app::tui::run is entered and an inline REPL is shown"
  tui10,"prompt-stays-print",xylitol 'fix the bug' is run,the process starts,print mode runs (not the TUI) because a prompt was given
  tui11,"abort-on-cancel",a long agent turn is streaming,the user presses the cancel key,"Driver::abort is called and the loop breaks cleanly"
  tui12,"scrollback-commit",a finalized text line exists,insert_before is called,the line appears in the terminal scrollback above the live viewport and is not redrawn on subsequent frames
  tui13,"textdelta-stream",a TextDelta event arrives,the tail is redrawn,the partial text is visible in the tail region and on a newline boundary is committed to scrollback
  tui13,"tool-status",a ToolExecutionStart then ToolExecutionEnd occur,the events are rendered,tool name and result preview appear without panicking
  tui14,"exit-command",the user types /exit,the command is parsed,the REPL exits cleanly restoring the terminal
  tui14,"model-command",the user types /model,the user types /model,"the model is switched via protocol::Command SetModel/CycleModel semantics"
  tui15,"restore-on-panic",the TUI panics during a turn,the panic unwinds,raw mode is disabled and the terminal is usable
  tui20,"no-umbrella-dep",Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change,dependency names are checked,"ratatui 0.30.x is absent and ratatui-core + ratatui-crossterm are present"
  tui21,"no-widget-imports",the TUI source under src/app/tui is inspected,import statements are checked,"no ratatui::widgets::* or ratatui_core::widgets::* built-in widget type (Paragraph/Block/List/Table) is imported; only Widget/StatefulWidget traits or Line/Text/Span leaf types are used"
  tui22,"flicker-reduced",a long streaming turn with frequent TextDelta newlines is rendered in the TUI,the terminal is observed,"insert_before commits do not produce visible clear-and-redraw jelly effect (scrolling-regions engaged)"
  tui30,"user-input-visible",the user types a prompt and presses Enter,the scrollback is inspected,the user's prompt text appears as a committed line above the live tail region
  tui31,"no-tail-linger",a streaming turn reaches TurnEnd,the frame after TurnEnd is rendered,the tail contains no leftover assistant text from the finished turn and the final line is in scrollback
  tui32,"no-floating-input",the TUI is idle with an empty input,the tail region is observed,the input area is visually anchored to the bottom edge with no ambiguous gap above it
